      {{/* this repo's own review gate — the three documented verbs only, never a bare
           `node bin/config-soak:*` wildcard, so a future subcommand is not pre-approved.
           Relative path because the ledger is anchored to the script's own location
           (REPO_ROOT = __dirname/..), so a worktree must run ITS copy: the invocation is always
           `cd <root> && node bin/config-soak <verb>`, and that compound form is what
           allow-compound-bash.sh matches (prefix only, no mid-path globs, so an absolute rule
           spanning every worktree under .claude cannot be written). Same relative-executable risk shape
           as the already-allowed ./gradlew and make. `land` is included deliberately: it lets
           Claude self-certify config it just wrote, trading the gate's independence for an
           unattended push — an explicit call by the repo owner, not an oversight. */}}
